## Summary
Gatik, a self-driving truck startup, raised $200 million in its largest funding round to date. The investment was led by Qatar Investment Authority and Koch Disruptive Technologies, following a deal with PepsiCo.

## Key Points
- Gatik secured $200 million in funding, marking its largest investment round.
- The funding round was led by Qatar Investment Authority and Koch Disruptive Technologies.
- The investment is associated with a partnership deal with PepsiCo.
- This underscores growing interest and investment in autonomous vehicle technology for logistics.


